cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use SentryTower, please cite it with these metadata.
title: "SentryTower: size-routed LLM security audits of source repositories"
type: software
authors:
  - name: The SentryTower Authors
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-14
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/National-Compute/sentrytower
abstract: >-
  SentryTower is an LLM security-audit harness. It counts the files of a
  repository and sends it to a funnel engine (1,000 files or fewer) or to a
  single agent (more). In its authors' own pre-registered test on the 117
  fresh security advisories with answer keys, an earlier internal build with
  GLM 5.3 Flash detected 29.1% of the vulnerabilities against 11.1% for
  Piolium, with the same model, budget and sandbox; the test does not
  measure a release or its default model.
keywords:
  - security
  - vulnerability detection
  - large language models
  - static analysis
  - SARIF
